Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:29:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] arm64: dts: qcom: pm8998: Describe the PMIC watchdog

The PON of PM8998 carries the PMIC watchdog. Describe it, with its bark
interrupt, and leave it disabled for boards to enable.

Written with an AI coding assistant (Claude); reviewed and tested as
described in the cover letter.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
index 3ecb33059..8b8730347 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm8998.dtsi
@@ -59,6 +59,12 @@ pm8998_resin: resin {
 				bias-pull-up;
 				status = "disabled";
 			};
+
+			pm8998_wdt: watchdog {
+				compatible = "qcom,pm8998-wdt";
+				interrupts = <0x0 0x8 6 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
 		};
 
 		pm8998_temp: temp-alarm@2400 {
-- 
